  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Songs of the Cossacks of the Kuban, where Black Sea Cossacks from the Zaporozhian lands of Ukraine settled at the end of the 18th century and kept a Ukrainian-based dialect (balachka) alongside the songs of the Russian line Cossacks. Historical, military, wedding and lyrical songs are sung by mixed village groups, and the Kuban Cossack Choir, directed from 1974 by Viktor Zakharchenko, staged and recorded the repertoire for Melodiya with bayan, balalaika and percussion.",
  "recipe": "classic Eastern European mid-1970s kuban cossack song, ballad Poetry, Slavic bard branch. global traditional polyphonic choir ensemble, b system buttons stradella bass Russian tradition song accompaniment chastushka dance bayan russian, melodic prima balalaika. moscow state label 1964-present major-flagship moscow melodiya studio. Neumann U47, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, Telefunken u73b broadcast comp, broadcast loudness EQ. tape 15ips hall reverb.",
